SUMMARY:Galapagos Islands Expedition ~ Untouched Nature in all its Splendo
 r! Small Group
DESCRIPTION:20s 30s Toronto Social & Activities\n***It's a Meetup . . . in
  the Galápagos!!***\n\n**This Meetup Event is for the nature lovers\, for
  the curious explorers and the adventurers who want to experience nature i
 n all its splendor & diversity.**\n\nThe Galápagos Islands are a volcanic
  archipelago in the Pacific Ocean\, considered one of the world's foremost
  destinations for wildlife-viewing. It's a place where lizards swim\, bird
 s walk\, and humans — for once — don't take center stage. In 1835 a 26
 -year-old Charles Darwin introduced the Galápagos Islands to the world wi
 th his theory of evolution.\n\nAs amazing as you think the Galápagos Isla
 nds would be\, they exceed all expectations of our group in 2023 and 2025!
  That sea lion above in our group photo is not a prop! It was very real\, 
 ready to play and pose for a picture. You can see sea lions\, giant lizard
 s and many other exotic and friendly creatures\, waddling on the streets\,
  playing in the sand or just chilling (sun bathing) on a bench!\n\n***We w
 ill explore and experience:***\n\n* The famous Galapagos penguin and blue 
 footed boobies. Swim with sea turtles and sea lions.\n* Tortuga Bay Beach 
 for swimming\, snorkeling\, kayaking or surfing with unique marine life.\n
 * Get close and personal with the giant tortoises roaming in their natural
  habitat\n* Explore the Tintoreras islet\, home of the white tip sharks an
 d its shark tunnel.\n* Visit the Charles Darwin Station\, to observe giant
  tortoises and their babies and learn about this majestic animal.\n* Snork
 eling around the shore of the Tijeretas Bay\n* Boat ride to Kicker Rock wi
 th snorkeling\n* Sailing to Santa Cruz Island.\n* Sail to Isabela Island\,
  the largest of the archipelago.\n* Boat tour to Tuneles De Cabo Rosa\, a 
 formation of series of above ocean arches\, creating an unique snorkeling 
 experience.\n* Explore cavernous underground Lava Tunnels.\n* Tour the Gal
 apagos rainforest habitat\n* San Cristobal Island with visit to the Interp
 retation Center\n* Visit to Los Gemelos\, a haven for bird watchers!\n* Vi
 sit Sierra Negra and Chico Volcano. A 10-mile challenging hike (for those 
 who are interested)\n* El Trapiche to see the old methods of extracting ca
 ne juice\, roasting coffee beans and techniques of distillery.\n* Quito wi
 th a full day tour and visit to the Equator line\n* Visit to the town of P
 uerto Baquerizo Moreno.\n\n***Land Tour cost US$4650 per person\, double o
 ccupancy***\n***(we match roommates for those wishing to share)***\n***Sol
 o occupancy additional US$990***\n**\\*\\*\\*Airfare not included\\*\\*\\*
 **\n\nWe have a second departure with the same itinerary: March 16-26\, 20
 27\n**[Click here to go to the event](https://www.meetup.com/moretoexplore
